bom-notes.md:66:Note added for firmware F3, 2026-11-10: the texts of GL1 (cover glass), CAP1 (joystick cap) and CAP2 (record cap) follow architecture 17.8: GL1 is one formed piece curved across the finger, 29.3 x 14.75 mm, 1.10 mm thick at its centre; CAP1 is a rounded rectangular nub 4.6 x 3.6 mm in a 6.4 x 5.4 mm frame at the bottom of the band; CAP2 is a pill 4.4 x 2.4 mm. Only the size and description cells of those three lines changed. Still at the 17.1 and 17.3 values on other lines and not touched here: the key_figures cell of CAP1 (switches at 1.9 mm, 3.1 mm inside; 17.3 says 2.1 mm and 3.6 mm), the HSG1 line (joystick opening 5.0 mm, record cap 5.0 x 3.0, shoulders 3.1 mm) and the cell, motor and pad lines (cell 1.6 x 6.0 x 38, 20 to 26 mAh; pads at 180 degrees). [History: the recording light parts and the nub were removed in v7, see the v7 note below.]
bom-notes.md:74:- One control: CAP2 (record button cap) is removed from the list; SW2 stays on BTN_REC as the switch under the centre of the joystick nub (CAP1). The item text of SW2 still contains the words "record button" because `tools/check_bom.py` matches the function name "Record button" of architecture section 2. [History: the recording light parts and the nub were removed in v7, see the v7 note below.]
bom-notes.md:77:- Microphone: SNR 67.5 dB(A), supply 1.62 to 3.60 V, bottom port, per `design/datasheets/mic-research/im68d128b-brief.txt` (architecture.md section 2 still says 68 dB(A)). R41 key figure now (3.0 V - 2.0 V) / 680 ohm = 1.5 mA (K16). Reference cells now hold one token per designator, separated by commas without spaces. [History: the recording light parts and the nub were removed in v7, see the v7 note below.]
bom-notes.md:85:- Recording light: R41 820 ohm; LED1 on the board's under face, pad 1 cathode; new lines LG1 (light guide) and LP1 (light plug). [History: the recording light parts and the nub were removed in v7, see the v7 note below.]
bom-notes.md:89:- Lines removed in v7: LED1, R41, LG1, LP1 and Q2 (the recording light, its resistor, its guide, its plug and its transistor). A recording shows on the screen (17.30). 82 part lines remain.
