ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:236:Checks replaced, old against new, and why: A5-1 (IM68D128B P1 to P5) became A7-3; A5-6 (Q1, D1, VDD_3V0) became A7-2; A6-1 (U2 order code empty, every ball provisional) became A7-1; A6-4 (67.5 dB(A) of the IM68D128B brief) became A7-6 (64.5 dB(A) of the Knowles sheet 2); A6-10 (Rev A6) became A7-10; the R41 check read W5 (680 ohm) and now reads 17.21 (820 ohm), because 17.21 replaces W5's value and W5 still says 680 (architecture line 284). A6-9 checks the motor line VMOT on the joystick tail in place of the pair MOTOR_DRV and VDD_3V0. Each old check described a state the five inputs remove; none was loosened. New: A7-4, A7-5, A7-8. [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:247:| order codes for C71, C85, C86, C87, C88, C35, C36, R41 | no maker sheet of a matching part is on file; no fetch was made. Each line has an empty code and an open action naming who answers | [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:256:6. U5, U6: 8-pad land pattern of Knowles sheet 6 at (-10.8, -4.8) and (10.8, -4.8), port facing the floor (mic-path items 31 to 33: build_board.py, check_board.py, R31, R32, Q2, R72 move). C35, C36 next to each Vdd pin; C31, C32 (Class 2) away from the microphones. [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:257:7. LED1 on the under face at X -9.70, Y -2.10, long side along Y, pad 1 = cathode (build_board.py line 70 maps it the other way); 0.50 mm non-plated hole at X -12.425, Y -2.95, no copper within 0.20 mm of its edge; keep the LG1 area free (light-path.md section 10, pcb row). [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:268:| 50 (not failing) | "Motor switch", "DMN2450UFB4" | the part stays only as the light transistor Q2; the row's function is out of date (17.22) | [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:279:| O11 | Order codes with maker sheets for C71 (1.0 uF 25 V), C85, C86, C87, C88, C35, C36 (Class 1 100 nF), R41 (820 ohm) | a distributor or the electronics designer | [History: the recording light and its parts were removed in v7, section 13.]
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:294:## 13. v7 changes (2026-11-11): the recording light removed in v7, round joystick
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:296:Contract: `design/architecture.md` 17.29 and 17.30 (17.30 wins over 17.21 and 17.22: "Recording light: removed. Out of the design: LED1, the light guide LG1, the light pipe LP1, the window in the glass print, the plug, R41 and Q2. The hole for the guide in the main board goes."), and the lead's fixed choices for v7 (round joystick, see `v7-wiring-notes.md`). Wiring revision A8 carries design v7. Evidence: `evidence/v7/`. Every part of that quote is removed in v7.
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:298:- Removed in v7 from the circuit: R41, LED1, Q2, their symbols LED_KPG1005 and DMN2450UFB4, the nets LED_A and LED_K. VDD_MIC keeps its real loads: U5, U6 and their capacitors C31, C32, C35, C36, plus C86 at the power chip's output (check A8-1). LED1, R41 and Q2 are listed as not placed in `additions.csv` and marked in `bom_refs_snapshot.csv` ("removed in v7").
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:301:- New checks: A8-1 (a list of references, symbols, nets and words that must not appear; proved to fail on a copy with R41 and LED1, removed in v7, put back), A8-2 (round joystick in the parts list). Removed: the R41 value check of 17.21, the check "no chip pin touches the light", A7-5. A7-10 became A8-10 (Rev A8).
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:302:- Counts after v7: `netlist.csv` 398 rows, 93 nets, 14 no-connect pins; `parts.csv` 118 parts; 25 symbols; `additions.csv` 44 added, 25 not placed, 22 test pads; `open-pins.csv` 60 rows (was 63: the three pins of Q2, removed in v7).
ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:303:- For the board (`pcb/`, not touched here): R41, LED1, Q2 are removed in v7; the 0.50 mm non-plated hole at X -12.425, Y -2.95 goes (no such hole is drawn in `pcb/ring.kicad_pcb` today). File and line list in `v7-wiring-notes.md`.
