mfg/specs/body.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v6.2 (architecture 17.11, 17.15, 17.19, 17.24 to 17.27; exterior merged32f, and merged32g on US 7 and US 8), and to design version 7 (architecture 17.29 and 17.30; exterior merged32h: round joystick opening 5.60 with the separate frame FRM1, gloss black finish; the recording light is removed in v7 and the body has no part of it). All dimensions in mm. Axes: X along the finger (+X fingertip), Y across (-Y is the joystick side, the side the thumb works; the older name "+Y thumb side" is retired, 17.11), Z up. Angles are measured around the finger from the top of the band; minus is the joystick side (the joystick is at -78 degrees on US 9 to 13, motor at -44 degrees on US 9; the values per ring size are in the last section).
mfg/specs/body.md:14:Titanium grade 5 (Ti-6Al-4V), machined from bar (architecture 17.29). Reason: strength at 0.4 to 0.6 mm walls, skin-safe, takes the gloss black coating. The joystick frame FRM1 is the same material and is coated in the same batch as the body (specs/joystick-nub.md).
mfg/specs/body.md:72:| joystick frame FRM1 | 5.40 mm outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long | ISO 2768-f on both diameters | separate part (specs/joystick-nub.md), bonded in the opening with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, 0.10 mm radial gap; 0.80 under the band surface to 0.50 above it |
mfg/specs/body.md:109:3. Clearance between the motor and its pocket: the design partner answers. The joystick clearances are fixed in v7: frame to opening 0.10 radial, cap to frame bore 0.20 radial (specs/joystick-nub.md).
mfg/specs/body.md:115:9. Closed in v7: the joystick opening is round, 5.60 diameter, through the wall, with the separate frame FRM1 (5.40 outer diameter, 1.30 long, 0.80 under the band surface to 0.50 above) bonded in it (17.29; specs/joystick-nub.md). History: the opening 6.6 along the finger by 5.6 around the band with a rectangular frame (17.24) is removed in v7.
