mfg/specs/cover-glass.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v5 (architecture 17.23, 17.24) and to design version 7 (architecture 17.30, 2026-11-11: the recording light is removed in v7). All dimensions in mm.
mfg/specs/cover-glass.md:6:The formed cover glass over the whole top face of the block. The face is one arc across the finger, rolled into the side walls and at the two ends. The screen under it stays flat. The glass is bonded to the screen panel by 0.1 mm clear adhesive (ADH1) over the whole face, so no air gap shows the edge of the lit area (17.30). It is also sealed to the body's glass seat all round by a perimeter seal ring SEAL1, 0.05 thick (Z 2.70 to 2.75), in a seat lowered 0.05 inside the body (model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24; open item S26). The tape is not chosen and its compressed thickness is unknown. Black print everywhere outside the lit area, with no opening of any kind in the print. History: the 0.4 mm print window for the recording light (17.21) is removed in v7 (17.30); the ring's recording sign is drawn on the screen by the firmware.
mfg/specs/cover-glass.md:59:4. Seal: the seal tape and its compressed thickness (S26). (Before v7 this point also held the recording light window; removed in v7, 17.30.)
mfg/specs/cover-glass.md:65:design/architecture.md lines 417, 419 (17.1), 488 (17.8, wins over 17.7 line 478); 17.23 and 17.24 (seal); 17.30 (the recording light is removed in v7, print with no opening, ADH1 over the whole face); design/architecture.md line 315 (16.1, lit area 10.8 x 21.6); design/bom.csv line 54; design/mech/thin/placement.csv (cover_glass).
mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:3:Design version 7 (2026-11-11): architecture 17.29 (round joystick, gloss black finish) and 17.30, on the exterior merged32h (`design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md`, all seven sizes `RESULT PASS`). Pocket, dam DAM1, stiffener and switch cross are unchanged from the inside model v6.3 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md` sections "Model v6" to "Model v6.3"). The file keeps its old name joystick-nub.md; the rectangular nub of version 6 and earlier is removed in v7 and replaced by the round cap CAP1. All dimensions in mm. "Along the finger" is X; "around the band" is the direction of the band's curve.
mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:90:- Maker files (inside model v7): design/mfg/parts/joystick-cap/joystick-cap.step and .stl (CAP1 with its flange, one solid) and design/mfg/parts/joystick-frame/joystick-frame.step and .stl (FRM1), both placed at the US 9 position (-78 deg); index.csv rows. The version 6 files (rectangular nub, removed in v7) are kept in design/mfg/parts/old_v63/ for history only: do not make anything from them.
mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:106:design/architecture.md 17.11 (one control, long press 1.0 s), 17.15 (cross 2.4), 17.24 and 17.26 (flange, roof, stiffener), 17.25 (angle per size), 17.29 (round joystick, finish), 17.30 (the recording light is removed in v7); design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md (opening, frame, cap and metal figures); design/bom.csv lines 39, 40, 81, 82; design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md sections "Model v6" to "Model v6.3"; 3M Scotch-Weld Epoxy Adhesive DP420 Black technical data sheet, revision June 2024, pages 1 and 3.
mfg/specs/main-board.md:3:Design version A5, architecture section 17.8 (2026-11-10), refreshed to the inside model v5 (architecture 17.19, 17.22, 17.24) and to design version 7 (architecture 17.30, 2026-11-11: the recording light and its parts are removed in v7, and the board has no hole). All dimensions in mm. Y: -Y is the joystick side.
mfg/specs/main-board.md:34:| holes through the board | 0 (none) | not a dimension | no drilled or routed hole in the outline; the non-plated light guide hole at X -12.425, Y -2.95 is removed in v7 (17.30), with LED1, R41 and Q2 removed in v7 |
mfg/specs/main-board.md:51:Drawing: design/mfg/drawings/main-board.svg and main-board.pdf. STEP and STL: design/mfg/parts/main-board/main-board.step and .stl (index.csv: bare PCB outline only, 27.2 x 12.6 x 0.28; the thickness in the STEP is 0.28, the architecture says 0.3: open point 8). That STEP file is from model v6.2 and still carries the light guide hole removed in v7; the lead regenerates it from the inside model v7, and until then this page wins: no hole. KiCad files: design/ecad (open: Gerber, drill and pick-and-place not made).
mfg/specs/main-board.md:63:10. Closed in v7: the board has no hole (17.30); the copper rule round the light guide hole, LED1, R41 and Q2 are removed in v7.
mfg/specs/v5-refresh-notes.md:3:Files: body.md, joystick-nub.md, main-board.md, cover-glass.md, band-flex-tails.md (all in design/mfg/specs/). Line numbers are the lines in the files as they stand now. Sources: TN = design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md (section Model v5, lines 99 to 200); AR = design/architecture.md section number (17.11, 17.15, 17.19, 17.21, 17.22, 17.23, 17.24); MP = design/mech/mic-path/mic-path.md; LP = design/mech/light-path/light-path.md; AS = design/mfg/assembly/assembly.md. No number was invented. Per-size values (motor angle, protection circuit start, floor slot depth) are written at US 9 with one sentence that the per-size value follows from the next model version (AR 17.24). Flange 6.9 and the 6.4 x 6.4 stiffener are written as "to follow" (AR 17.24 rulings K12, K13).
mfg/specs/v5-refresh-notes.md:7:- joystick-nub.md:6 "record button": "the ring has no record button". Also "Before v5: four switches in a cross at 2.1 mm at +150 degrees" (former value, named).
