mfg/specs/v7-refresh-notes.md:20:- ISO 2768-1 gives no general tolerance under 0.5 mm. joystick-nub.md sets: ridge height 0.08 +-0.02; ridge width, dish depth, edge radius, flange thickness +-0.05; frame top 0.50 +-0.05. Tagged [PROPOSED].
mfg/specs/v7-refresh-notes.md:26:- No v7 inside model is measured yet. The total length of CAP1 and the opening's wall length between frame and roof have no accepted figure; joystick-nub.md open point 8 says the inside model v7 gives them.
mfg/specs/v7-refresh-notes.md:27:- The maker files and drawings in `design/mfg/parts/` and `design/mfg/drawings/` are still v6.2. `draw.py` lines 40 to 52 still list the light parts and the rectangular frame (not mine).
mfg/specs/record-cap.md:5:A recording starts and stops by a long press of 1.0 s on the joystick's centre switch SW2 (architecture 17.11; specs/joystick-nub.md).
mfg/part-map.csv:4:joystick-nub,CAP1,"Joystick cap CAP1, round, with its 6.90 x 6.40 flange (one moulded part; design v7, folder name kept)"
mfg/parts-notes.md:3:> **Design version 7 (2026-11-11, architecture 17.29 to 17.31): these files ARE v7.** They were written from the inside model v7 (round joystick: cap CAP1 and frame FRM1; no recording light; no board hole) on the accepted exterior merged32h at every size. The v6 files of the removed parts (joystick-nub, light-guide, light-plug) and the v6.2 index are kept in `parts/old_v63/` for history only: do not make anything from them.
mfg/parts-notes.md:25:- **cover-glass** (STEP): the exterior's formed glass. Its print has no opening in v7 (the print window is removed in v7); the print is not geometry.
mfg/parts-notes.md:26:- **joystick-cap** (STEP and STL): CAP1, the round cap: shank dia 4.40 with its rounded top edge, spherical dish and three ridges, and its 6.90 x 6.40 x 0.40 flange; one moulded part, written as two touching solids (shank and flange, 78.7324 mm3 together). Placed at the US 9 position (-78 deg); the same part at every size (the shank from the flange top to the rim plane is 4.110 to 4.118 mm in the seven size builds, within the model's 0.01 surface probe step; export logs, line "joystick US"). Spec: `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
mfg/parts-notes.md:27:- **joystick-frame** (STEP and STL): FRM1, the round frame ring, outer dia 5.40, bore 4.80, 1.30 long; placed at the US 9 position. Spec: `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:3:Basis: first written on design commit a0cf952 (2026-11-11, 00:50 to 01:00); brought to the inside model v6 and architecture 17.22 to 17.26 on the working tree at commit 6ccb258 or later (2026-11-11, from 05:38), what changed then is in `design/mfg/assembly/v6-update-notes.md`; brought to design version 7 on 2026-11-11 (architecture 17.29 and 17.30: round joystick cap CAP1 in a bonded round frame FRM1, gloss black finish; the recording light and its parts are removed in v7), what changed is in `design/mfg/assembly/v7-update-notes.md`. Step numbers are unchanged since the first issue, so other files that cite a step stay right. Each citation below was re-read by `check_assembly.py`, which prints the cited line (check.log).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:23:Where files show an older state. The last measured inside model is v6.3 (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:407`); the inside model v7 (no light parts, round joystick) is being built by the lead and is not yet measured. The exterior of v7 is merged32h (`design/look/s1/merged32h-report.md:70`). The maker files in `design/mfg/parts/` are still v6.2 (they still hold the light parts removed in v7 and the rectangular joystick removed in v7); the lead regenerates them. The specs in `design/mfg/specs/` are brought to v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:1`). This file follows architecture 17.11 to 17.30 wherever an older file differs, and says so at each step.
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:63:| Joystick frame | FRM1 | round titanium ring, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black with the body, bonded in the round 5.60 opening with DP420 Black | `design/architecture.md:826`, `design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:1` | 13 |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:78:Not used: the record cap CAP2 and its opening (removed, `design/architecture.md:546`); the wall microphone slots (removed, `design/architecture.md:657`); the recording light with LED1, R41, Q2, the light guide LG1 and the light plug LP1, the print window and the board hole, all removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`); the rectangular joystick nub and frame, removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:826`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:91:- **Check:** the board maker's electrical test of every net, thickness, warp (`design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:45`); no hole through the board (`design/mfg/specs/main-board.md:34`; the light guide hole is removed in v7).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:96:- **Join:** every board part of `design/bom.csv` to the under face of PCB1, with solder paste and one reflow. The parts: U1 (`main_chip`), U2 (`power_chip`, nPM1304, `design/architecture.md:566`), R71, R72, U3 (`storage`), U10, U4 (`screen_supply_chip`), U5 (`mic_1`) and U6 (`mic_2`), Knowles SPK0641HT4H-1 (`design/architecture.md:654`, `design/bom.csv:9`), J1 (`screen_connector`), ANT1 (`antenna`), L2, L3, L4, C3, C12, X1 (`crystal_32M`), X2 (`crystal_32k`), L1, FB1, R1, R2, C1, C2, C5, C4, C6, C7, C10, C14, C11, L10 (`screen_supply_coil`), C21, C26, C27, C24, C25, C23, C22, C28, C29, C31, C32, C35, C36, R31, R32, R57, R58, R60, C60, U11 (`motor_regulator`, TLV75530PDQNR, at X 0.0, Y 4.2), C83 (`motor_cap_in`, X 0.0, Y 5.45), C84 (`motor_cap_out`, X 1.2, Y 5.0) (`design/architecture.md:705`, `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:19` to `design/mech/thin/placement.csv:21`; the places are the model's proposal until the board layout confirms them, `design/architecture.md:760`), U9, R61 and R62 (now on U11's enable pin, `design/architecture.md:705`), R66, R63, R64, R65, C61, C72, C80, C81, C82, C71, C73, C74, C75, C78, C79, C76, C77, C85, C86, C87, C88 (`design/bom.csv:67` to `design/bom.csv:69`), L71 (`power_coil_1`), L72 (`power_coil_2`). The motor switch and the motor diode of earlier versions are not fitted: they left the design (`design/architecture.md:705`). LED1, R41 and Q2 are removed in v7 and are not fitted (`design/architecture.md:834`). The test pads TP1 to TP22 (TP1, TP2, TP3, TP4, TP5, TP6, TP7, TP8, TP9, TP10, TP11, TP12, TP13, TP14, TP15, TP16, TP17, TP18, TP19, TP20, TP21, TP22) and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B are copper on the same face and get no paste [PROPOSED: reason, a solder bump on a test pad or a hot-bar land spoils the spring-pin contact and the hot-bar joint of step 16]. C13 is not mounted (`design/bom.csv:18`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:112:- **Join:** nothing is joined. The under face of PCB1 is cleaned of flux residue round the test pads TP1 to TP22 and the ribbon lands J_BAND_A and J_BAND_B, then dried [PROPOSED: reason, the spring pins of step 5 and the hot-bar joints of step 16 need bare copper; the paste and flux of step 2 are not named by any file]. History: this step fitted the light guide LG1 until v6; the light guide is removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:185:- **Join:** first the frame FRM1 (titanium grade 5, 5.40 outer diameter, 4.80 bore, 1.30 long, coated gloss black in the same batch as the body) is bonded into the round 5.60 opening from outside the band with 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black epoxy, 0.10 mm radial gap filled all round (`design/bom.csv:82`, `design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`). Cure: 24 h at 22 C with no heat, the room temperature cure of 3M's data sheet for DP420 Black (revision June 2024, page 3: 4,500 psi overlap shear on aluminium after 24 h at 22 C); no oven, because the membranes of step 11 and the gaskets of step 12 are already in the body. Then the round cap CAP1 (`joystick_cap`, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510, shank 4.40 and flange as one moulded part, `design/bom.csv:81`) goes in straight from the bore: the 6.90 x 6.40 flange rises through the 7.0 x 6.8 pocket (0.05 mm on each side along the finger, 0.2 mm round the band), the 4.40 shank passes up through the 4.80 bore of FRM1 with 0.20 mm radial clearance, and the flange stops under the pocket roof, 0.05 mm below it, held on all four sides by the roof round the 5.60 opening (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:249`, `design/architecture.md:826`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:187:- **Before:** steps 10 to 12 passed. FRM1 and the body were coated in the same batch (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:22`). The bonding faces are degreased with isopropyl alcohol [PROPOSED: reason, the coated faces carry handling oil]. The DP420 has cured 24 h at 22 C before CAP1 goes in, because the cap is centred by the frame's bore and the frame must not move. The harness is not yet in the channel: the cap must go in before the switch head, which lies under the flange on the bore side (`design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md:255`).
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:257:- **Join:** nothing is joined. The body's glass seat and the screen's top face are cleaned with isopropyl alcohol and lint-free wipes, then blown with ionised air [PROPOSED: reason, the cast of step 21 runs next to the block, and a speck on the seat breaks the line of SEAL1 while a speck on the screen shows under ADH1]. History: this step placed the light plug LP1 until v6; the light plug is removed in v7 (`design/architecture.md:834`).
