mfg/assembly/assembly.md:340:| 4 | Print of the cover glass | no opening: the print window is removed in v7 (`design/mfg/specs/cover-glass.md:6`) | nothing beyond row 1 | yes, it adds no path |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:367:| Adhesive of the joystick frame: fixed, 3M Scotch-Weld DP420 Black, 24 h at 22 C | 13 | fixed in v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:23`); bench B9 proves the bond on the coated titanium | B9 |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:369:| Cap CAP1 and frame FRM1: fixed, Makrolon 2407 colour 901510 moulded; Ti-6Al-4V turned, separate part | 13 | fixed in v7 (`design/mfg/specs/joystick-nub.md:16`); a moulder and the body maker quote (`design/bom.csv:81`, `design/bom.csv:82`) | B9 |
mfg/assembly/assembly.md:395:RESULT: done, 28 numbered steps (numbers unchanged) brought to design version 7 (architecture 17.29 and 17.30): no step fits a light guide or a light plug (both removed in v7, steps 4 and 22 now clean and inspect), step 13 bonds the frame FRM1 with DP420 Black (24 h at 22 C) and then fits the round cap CAP1 with its flange from the bore; of 12 conflict rows 4 are closed (K-A4, K-A7, K-A10, K-A11), 3 changed (K-A1, K-A3, K-A6), 5 open (K-A2, K-A5, K-A8, K-A9, K-A12); no water or dust rating can be claimed today; the check script passes (v7-check.log).
mfg/mfg-notes.md:5:Old states, for reference only: `parts/old_v63/` (the v6 joystick nub, the light guide LG1 and light plug LP1, all removed in v7, and the v6.2 index), `drawings/old_v63/` (their sheets); `parts/old_merged32c/`, `drawings/old_merged32c/` (the older exterior). Do not make anything from them.
mfg/mfg-notes.md:13:- What draw.py cannot do: dimension an inside feature on the views. It draws the outline with hidden edges dashed and dimensions only the overall size; the pockets, slots, roof and the motor window are given in each body sheet's table (values from the model), the cap and frame dimensions in `specs/joystick-nub.md`.
